4.1. Motivating example
In the subsequent sections, we delve into strategies for accelerating inference latency, or equivalently, increasing the TPS count. While various techniques exist for optimizing Large Language Model (LLM) inference, including intelligent decoding methods (
[Leviathan et al. 2023](#bib.bib17)
;
[Santilli et al. 2023](#bib.bib29)
) , improved memory access patterns (
[Kwon et al. 2023](#bib.bib16)
;
[Dao et al. 2022](#bib.bib7)
) , and model compression and quantization (
[Frantar et al. 2022](#bib.bib12)
;
[Xiao et al. 2023](#bib.bib36)
) , among others, this paper introduces an orthogonal approach specifically tailored for schema matching acceleration, known as
*prompt compression*
. Our approach is inspired by the observation that the inference time T T for transformer-based LLMs is quadratic to the input length L input L_{\mathrm{input}} , i.e., T = 𝒪 ⁡ ( L input 2 ) T=\mathcal{O}(L_{\mathrm{input}}^{2}) . This is because the self-attention output is computed as

